[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477399160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3477399160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3477399160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PROZ4","user":{"login":"AdvanceControl","id":163237388,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbrODA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163237388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl","html_url":"https://github.com/AdvanceControl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T03:32:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T03:32:57Z","body":"This is not a bug. \nTo fix this problem, you can call the FileAccess.flush method.\nFor example:\n``` GDScript\n\tvar file_access: FileAccess = FileAccess.open(file_path, FileAccess.READ_WRITE)\n\tprint(\"Opened \", FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 4\n\tfile_access.resize(0)\n\tprint(\"Resized \", FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 0\n\tfile_access.store_32(0)\n\tfile_access.flush()\n\tprint(\"Stored \", FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 4\n\tfile_access.seek(0)\n\tprint(\"Seeked \", FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 4\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477399160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477426261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3477426261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3477426261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PRVBV","user":{"login":"Lexyth","id":18605122,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjA1MTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18605122?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth","html_url":"https://github.com/Lexyth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T04:06:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T04:06:33Z","body":"Oh, so every call to seek flushes behind the scenes... Good to know.\n\nBut why is get_size returning only the flushed size not a bug?\nThe description says the same as that of get_length, which returns the size after flushing (since it's based on seek).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477426261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477495976","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3477495976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3477495976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PRmCo","user":{"login":"AdvanceControl","id":163237388,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbrODA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163237388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl","html_url":"https://github.com/AdvanceControl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdvanceControl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T06:28:15Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T06:28:26Z","body":"Before the flush method is called, the written data is stored in the buffer. \nThe get_size method will load the file size from the disk (at this point, the data in the buffer has not been written to the file, so it will return an incorrect result)\n\nget_length method reads the file size from the memory.\n\nUsing another FileAccess to open the file and calling get_length would also return an incorrect result.\n\n``` GDScript\nvar file_path := \"res://test\"\nFileAccess.open(file_path, FileAccess.WRITE)\nvar file_access: FileAccess = FileAccess.open(file_path, FileAccess.READ_WRITE)\n\nfile_access.store_32(0)\nprint(FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 0\nvar new_file := FileAccess.open(file_path,FileAccess.READ)\nprint(new_file.get_length()) # 0\nprint(file_access.get_length()) # 4\n\nfile_access.flush()\nprint(FileAccess.get_size(file_path)) # 4\nprint(new_file.get_length()) # 4\nprint(file_access.get_length()) # 4\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477495976/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3480179003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3480179003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3480179003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Pb1E7","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-03T12:02:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-03T12:02:26Z","body":"I'd say we should add a warning to the documentation to not use `get_size` for a file you're currently operating on but instead use the correct `get_length`. Using `get_size` is probably worse for performance as well as it has to actually fetch the information from the file system","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3480179003/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3480280838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3480280838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3480280838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PcN8G","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-03T12:28:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-03T12:28:18Z","body":"> Oh, so every call to seek flushes behind the scenes... Good to know.\n\nNot necessarily, a file is always flushed when you call `flush` or when a file is closed (last reference to `FileAccess` is removed). It can be flushed in other conditions as well, but it depends on platform, file system, and other conditions outside control, so you should not rely on it.\n\n`get_size` exist to get file size without opening a file, and should not be used if a file is already opened.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3480280838/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488166763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3488166763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3488166763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7P6TNr","user":{"login":"Lexyth","id":18605122,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjA1MTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18605122?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth","html_url":"https://github.com/Lexyth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T22:03:12Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T22:03:12Z","body":"> I'd say we should add a warning to the documentation to not use `get_size` for a file you're currently operating on but instead use the correct `get_length`. Using `get_size` is probably worse for performance as well as it has to actually fetch the information from the file system\n\nI can confirm that `get_size` performs worse than `get_length`, the latter being near identical to manually seeking to the end and back to the original position (which is probably all it does, but I didn't confirm that), at least up to 10MB; the difference remained constant, so I'm not sure if it may stay so regardless of file size, as that can have an effect on seek with very large files.\n\nAnd I do agree that it needs a warning. I was hesitant to use `get_size` because I wasn't sure whether the size metadata was only updated on flush (which I assumed was only automatically called on close or manually) or would always be updated on write.Turns out, it *is* updated on flush, which makes perfect sense, but seek calling flush surprised me. That also can make sense, but, I think, it should also get a warning or note mentioning it, since it's an implementation detail, that, as far as I managed to gather, is not always required when seeking; might be wrong there, but it would still be nice to have it explicitly mentioned. Even if it's perfectly valid behavior, it's very unintuitive that every seek call triggers a flush, especially given the \"flushing often reduces performance\" warning in the documentation of the flush method itself.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488166763/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488197378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112303#issuecomment-3488197378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112303","id":3488197378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7P6asC","user":{"login":"Lexyth","id":18605122,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjA1MTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18605122?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth","html_url":"https://github.com/Lexyth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lexyth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T22:15:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T22:15:26Z","body":"> > Oh, so every call to seek flushes behind the scenes... Good to know.\n> \n> Not necessarily\n\nI'm not sure I understand what you mean. Is the flushing on seek conditional?\nWhen I took a cursory glance at what I assumed to be the effective implementation of seek, I didn't even see the flushing part; it seemed to only update the position. I don't know cpp syntax, though, so a lot of what's going on there feels like magic to me anyway.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488197378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]